From: mscharged-port
Subject: Tweak: recorded matches keep the game's stats
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

The game counts every player's shots, goals, assists, passes, hits, steals,
items and more for the match (StatsTracker, which the Cup and the stats
screens read); every count goes through StatsTracker::TrackStat. A recorded
match (tweak patch 0071) now keeps those totals in its replay, with the
moments the launcher's match stats show: each goal (scorer, assist, kind),
shot, Skillshot, Mega Strike, item, hit, steal and foul, when and where the
player stood. ThrowPowerup tells the item's type and how many first, which
TrackStat's STATS_POWERUPS_USED does not.

The hooks only read: src/platform/match_stats.cpp keeps the moments (online,
those of the steps the rollback undoes go again) and reads the totals.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_replay.h b/include/mscharged_replay.h
index 86c87d4..3774686 100644
--- a/include/mscharged_replay.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_replay.h
@@ -66,6 +66,12 @@ bool mscharged_tweak_presentation_test_press(void);
 // network match (the game skips the part once nothing holds it: a score that
 // still counts); at each update until the part ends.
 void mscharged_tweak_presentation_pressed(int part);
+// Match stats (tweak patch 0085): a recorded match keeps what the game
+// counted for each player (its StatsTracker) and the moments that matter.
+// StatsTracker::TrackStat, as it counts a stat (before it does).
+void mscharged_tweak_stats_tracked(int stat, int side, int player, int param0, int param1, int param2, int param3);
+// ThrowPowerup, as a player throws or uses an item: its type and how many.
+void mscharged_tweak_stats_item(int side, int player, int type, int count);
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
